flowchart LR
    Pkt["packet at Netfilter hook<br/><b>does:</b> presents 5-tuple, zone, direction<br/><b>why next:</b> conntrack needs a tuple key<br/><b>state:</b> skb may not yet have nfct"]
    Tuple["tuple extraction<br/><b>does:</b> parses L3/L4 headers and reply tuple<br/><b>why next:</b> hash lookup uses normalized original/reply keys<br/><b>state:</b> tuplehash candidate"]
    Lookup["conntrack lookup<br/><b>does:</b> searches confirmed table for either direction<br/><b>why next:</b> existing flow can update state; miss may create NEW<br/><b>state:</b> nf_conn found or miss"]
    Existing["existing entry<br/><b>does:</b> updates TCP/UDP/ICMP state and timeout<br/><b>why next:</b> rules need ct state labels<br/><b>state:</b> ESTABLISHED/RELATED/INVALID etc. on skb"]
    New["unconfirmed NEW entry<br/><b>does:</b> allocates nf_conn and attaches it to skb<br/><b>why next:</b> later verdict decides whether it becomes visible<br/><b>state:</b> skb->nfct points at unconfirmed ct"]
    Rules["filter/NAT rules<br/><b>does:</b> match ct state, may DNAT/SNAT, may DROP<br/><b>why next:</b> only accepted first packets should be confirmed<br/><b>state:</b> verdict and possibly translated tuple"]
    Confirm["nf_conntrack_confirm<br/><b>does:</b> inserts accepted NEW ct into global hash<br/><b>why next:</b> replies/future packets can find it<br/><b>state:</b> confirmed conntrack entry"]
    Drop["DROP/invalid/stress path<br/><b>does:</b> frees or leaves entry unconfirmed<br/><b>state:</b> no reusable flow state"]

    Pkt --> Tuple --> Lookup
    Lookup -->|hit| Existing --> Rules
    Lookup -->|miss| New --> Rules
    Rules -->|ACCEPT first packet| Confirm
    Rules -->|DROP or invalid| Drop

    classDef parse fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb
    classDef ct fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706
    classDef out fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a
    classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626
    class Pkt,Tuple parse
    class Lookup,Existing,New,Rules ct
    class Confirm out
    class Drop bad
